rado, Uncompahgre Plateau and Dallas Divide.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is likely with additional rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms expected through Thursday night. The potential for\nflooding impacts continues into Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:53PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Ouray County in southwestern Colorado...\nNorth Central San Juan County in southwestern Colorado...\nEast Central San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT Tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1250 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain due to thunderstorms. Flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly in the warned area. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches\nof rain have fallen over the last 24 hours so any heavy rainfall\non already saturated areas could result in rockslides or\nmudslides in already steep terrain.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nTelluride, Mountain Village, Ouray, Ophir, Camp Bird, Black Bear\n